From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 16:20:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-drm: add the max bpc connector property

KWin, like other compositors, uses the standard "max bpc" connector
property to limit the output bit depth: to save link bandwidth, to keep
8 bpc on docks where more is unreliable, or because the user picked a
limit in the display settings. nvidia-drm didn't have it, so the
compositor could neither limit nor offer the setting.

NVKMS has no notion of a limit, only of an exact bpc in the modeset
request, which also changes the ioctl ABI that NVIDIA's userspace uses.
Add a per-display attribute instead,
NV_KMS_DPY_ATTRIBUTE_REQUESTED_COLOR_BPC_MAX, stored like the requested
color range. A modeset that doesn't
request a specific bpc first picks the color format and bpc as before,
then lowers the bpc to the limit in the same format (nvLimitColorBpcEvo),
and leaves it unspecified so mode validation can still lower it further
to fit the link. It never goes below what the colorimetry needs (10 bpc
for BT.2100), and the attribute path that recomputes the bpc when the
color format or range changes applies the limit too.

nvidia-drm attaches "max bpc" (8-12) to the connectors that have Broadcast
RGB. Like the color range it is applied by a modeset: DRM core flags the
CRTC when it changes, and the value is passed to KAPI with every modeset,
so a display newly driven by a CRTC, or recreated by a hotplug, gets it
as well. KAPI stores it on the displays at commit; a limit can only lower
the bpc, so a TEST_ONLY check without it is never too permissive. Values
NVKMS doesn't drive (9, 11) are rounded down. The connector state hooks
set the default, which the DRM state helpers leave at 0.

To verify what is actually programmed, add a debugfs file per connector,
current_bpc: the bpc NVKMS currently drives the display with
(NV_KMS_DPY_ATTRIBUTE_CURRENT_COLOR_BPC) and the limit NVKMS has stored
for it, both through a new KAPI query. DRM core's output_bpc file in the
same directory shows the maximum the display supports.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
